// ChainIssueCode - EMPTY_CHAIN: fewer than min_functions
//   - MAX_FUNCTIONS_EXCEEDED / TYPE_LIMIT_EXCEEDED: above a domain policy limit (not a resource shortage)
//   - DUPLICATE_INSTANCE_ID: duplicated instance_id
//   - FUNCTION_UNAVAILABLE: no VVF in the TED provides the type
//   - VVF_INCOMPLETE: the functions of a require_all VVF are not all there (e.g. color alone).
//     Checked per VVF instance (one End.AN; a repeated type is another instance):
//     a lone color after a complete color / transcode / crop makes the second instance incomplete.
//     instance_id is the first function of that instance
//   - VVF_NOT_CONTIGUOUS: another function sits between the functions of one VVF
//   - VVF_ORDER: the functions of an ordered VVF are out of order
//   - VVF_NODE_REQUIRED: a function of a `pinned` VVF has no `vvf_node_id`
//   - VVF_NODE_UNKNOWN: `vvf_node_id` is not a node of the VVF (also when given for a `dynamic` VVF)
//   - FORMAT_MISMATCH: a function's input format does not match, or the chain output does not match the domain policy's output format
//     (e.g. a chain without transcode in a domain with 8K DG input)
//   - INVALID_PARAMS: invalid parameters
//
// Example: VVF_INCOMPLETE
type ChainIssueCode string

